  <main id="main">

    <section class="page-head">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Pricing</span>
        <h1>Clear pricing. <em>No guesswork.</em></h1>
        <p class="lead">Starting prices for every kind of project, an honest list of what changes the cost, and every ongoing cost spelled out before you agree to anything.</p>
        <div class="btn-row page-head__cta">
          <a href="start" class="btn btn--primary" data-track="cta-pricing-estimate">Get an estimate</a>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-review-open data-track="cta-pricing-tell">Not sure what you need?</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- AT A GLANCE -->
    <section class="section" id="starting" aria-labelledby="startTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">At a glance</span>
          <h2 id="startTitle">What things cost.</h2>
          <p>Starting prices. Your proposal fixes the exact scope and price before any development. Outside South Africa? We quote in USD, EUR or GBP.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="glance reveal">
          <div class="price-group" id="websites">
            <h3>Build one thing</h3>
            <p class="glance__sub">A fixed price for a defined scope.</p>
            <ul class="price-list price-list--compact">
              <li><a href="ai-demos">AI solution<small>One focused tool, e.g. answers from your own documents</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R25,000</span></li>
              <li><a href="ai-for-business#library">Automation<small>One repetitive task handled across your tools</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R15,000</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#dashboards">Dashboard<small>Your key numbers in one live view</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R15,000</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#software">Custom software<small>Tools, portals and integrations built around you</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R45,000</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#websites">Business website<small>Custom design, up to 8 pages, SEO set-up</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R12,500</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#websites">Platform or web app<small>Bookings, payments, client portals</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R35,000</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="price-group">
            <h3>Automate a whole process</h3>
            <p class="glance__sub">In stages, and you can stop after any of them.</p>
            <ul class="price-list price-list--compact">
              <li><a href="#implementation">Discovery<small>We map the work and measure it today &middot; 1&ndash;2 weeks &middot; credited if you go ahead</small></a><span class="price">R15,000</span></li>
              <li><a href="#implementation">Proof of concept<small>A small working version, tested on real work &middot; 2&ndash;4 weeks</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R35,000</span></li>
              <li><a href="#implementation">Production<small>Connected to your systems, documented, your team trained</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R85,000</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="price-group" id="care">
            <h3>Keep it running</h3>
            <p class="glance__sub">Monthly, listed in your proposal.</p>
            <ul class="price-list price-list--compact">
              <li><span class="pl-name">Managed hosting<small>Secure, backed up, monitored</small></span><span class="price">R450<span class="per">/mo</span></span></li>
              <li><span class="pl-name">Care<small>Hosting plus an hour of changes a month</small></span><span class="price">R1,450<span class="per">/mo</span></span></li>
              <li><a href="#operations">Operate<small>One AI system watched, fixed and reported on</small></a><span class="price">R7,500<span class="per">/mo</span></span></li>
              <li><a href="#operations">Optimise<small>Up to three systems, improved every month</small></a><span class="price">R15,000<span class="per">/mo</span></span></li>
              <li><a href="#operations">Partner<small>All your systems, fastest response</small></a><span class="price">R35,000<span class="per">/mo</span></span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- WORKED EXAMPLE -->
    <section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="fyTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">A worked example</span>
          <h2 id="fyTitle">What it costs, and when it pays back.</h2>
          <p>Example numbers for enquiry handling at a 40-person firm. Yours come from your own baseline in discovery.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ex reveal">
          <table class="spec">
            <caption>Cost</caption>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Discovery</td><td class="price">R15,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Proof of concept</td><td class="price">R35,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Production implementation</td><td class="price">R85,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Less discovery credit</td><td class="price">−R15,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Implementation, total</strong></td><td class="price"><strong>R120,000</strong></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Operations (Operate)</td><td class="price">R7,500/mo</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <table class="spec">
            <caption>Value</caption>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>8 people × 10 hours a week on enquiries</td><td class="price">346 h/mo</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Share the system takes over (measured)</td><td class="price">60%</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Hours back</td><td class="price">208 h/mo</td></tr>
              <tr><td>At R28,000 salary (loaded ≈ R210/h)</td><td class="price">R43,730/mo</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Less operations</td><td class="price">−R7,500/mo</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Payback</strong></td><td class="price"><strong>≈ 3.3 months</strong></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="center small muted section__foot reveal">Hours × loaded cost (salary × 1.3 ÷ 173). Revenue effects such as faster replies winning more work are reported separately, and only when measured. <a class="inline-link" href="method#measure">How we measure</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ ROI CALCULATOR ============ -->
    <section class="section" id="roi" aria-labelledby="roiTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Is it worth it?</span>
          <h2 id="roiTitle">What is that work costing you?</h2>
          <p>A rough estimate in ten seconds. Discovery replaces it with a measured one.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="roi reveal" data-roi>
          <div class="roi__inputs">
            <label class="roi__field"><span>People doing this work</span><output data-roi-out="people">3</output><input type="range" name="people" min="1" max="50" value="3" /></label>
            <label class="roi__field"><span>Hours each spends on it per week</span><output data-roi-out="hours">5</output><input type="range" name="hours" min="1" max="40" value="5" /></label>
            <label class="roi__field"><span>Their monthly salary (R)</span><output data-roi-out="salary">R25,000</output><input type="range" name="salary" min="8000" max="120000" step="1000" value="25000" /></label>
            <label class="roi__field"><span>Share of that work a system could take over</span><output data-roi-out="share">60%</output><input type="range" name="share" min="20" max="90" step="5" value="60" /></label>
          </div>
          <div class="roi__out" aria-live="polite">
            <div><span>Hours back every month</span><b data-roi="hours">0</b></div>
            <div><span>Value of that time, per month</span><b data-roi="month">R0</b></div>
            <div class="roi__big"><span>Per year</span><b data-roi="year">R0</b></div>
            <p class="tiny muted">Hours × loaded cost (salary × 1.3 ÷ 173 hours). An estimate, not a promise: we measure the real figure in discovery.</p>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary btn--full" data-review-open data-track="cta-roi">Tell us about it</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <form class="sendme reveal" data-sendme="roi" novalidate>
          <p class="sendme__t">Keep this estimate? We&rsquo;ll email you the numbers.</p>
          <div class="sendme__row">
            <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required placeholder="you@company.com" aria-label="Your email address" />
            <input type="text" name="business" autocomplete="organization" placeholder="Business (optional)" aria-label="Business name (optional)" />
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn--primary btn--small">Email it to me</button>
          </div>
          <input type="text" name="_gotcha" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px;width:1px;height:1px;opacity:0" />
          <p class="tiny muted sendme__msg" data-sendme-msg aria-live="polite">We&rsquo;ll send it once and may follow up once. <a class="inline-link" href="privacy">Privacy</a></p>
        </form>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- IMPLEMENTATION -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="implementation" aria-labelledby="implTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Larger AI process work</span>
          <h2 id="implTitle">When the job is bigger than a fixed-scope build.</h2>
          <p>Automating a whole process across your software is done in stages you can stop between. Each stage ends with something you keep and a decision, and nothing goes to production before it has proved itself on your work.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="stages reveal">
          <li><div><span class="stages__k">Start here</span><h3>Process review</h3><p>30 minutes. Where the time goes, whether AI is the answer, and what we&rsquo;d look at first.</p></div><b>Free</b></li>
          <li><div><span class="stages__k">Phases 1–2 · 1–2 weeks</span><h3>Discovery &amp; opportunity map</h3><p>Process map, baseline measurements, every opportunity scored, an ROI estimate and a recommended first build. Yours to keep. Credited in full against implementation if you go ahead within 60 days.</p></div><b>R15,000</b></li>
          <li><div><span class="stages__k">Phases 3–4 · 2–4 weeks</span><h3>Proof of concept</h3><p>The smallest useful version, on real work, measured before vs after. Go, adjust or stop.</p></div><b><small>from</small> R35,000</b></li>
          <li><div><span class="stages__k">Phases 5–6 · fixed quote</span><h3>Production implementation</h3><p>Integrated with your software, with permissions, logging and safe fallbacks, documented, and your team trained.</p></div><b><small>from</small> R85,000</b></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="small muted section__foot reveal">A 40% deposit starts each paid stage and comes off its price; the balance is due on completion. Larger implementations can be split across milestones. <a class="inline-link" href="terms">Terms</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- OPERATIONS -->
    <section class="section" id="operations" aria-labelledby="opsTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Operations</span>
          <h2 id="opsTitle">Run, measured and improved, every month.</h2>
          <p>Starts at go-live, with a 3-month minimum and then month to month. Every plan includes monitoring, AI usage up to its allowance, maintenance, security updates, usage monitoring, evaluation, support to the SLA, improvement hours, and a monthly ROI report.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid plans plans--3">
          <div class="card plan reveal">
            <h3>Operate</h3>
            <div class="plan__price">R7,500<small>/month</small></div>
            <p>For one system: we keep it working, fix what breaks and show you the results every month.</p>
            <ul><li>1 system covered</li><li>AI usage (what the AI provider charges) up to R1,500 a month</li><li>2 hours a month for optimisation</li><li>Accuracy check every quarter, against real examples</li><li>Monthly ROI report</li><li>Support: next business day</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card plan plan--featured reveal">
            <span class="plan__flag">Most chosen</span>
            <h3>Optimise</h3>
            <div class="plan__price">R15,000<small>/month</small></div>
            <p>For up to three systems: everything in Operate, plus time each month to make them better.</p>
            <ul><li>Up to 3 systems</li><li>AI usage (what the AI provider charges) up to R4,000 a month</li><li>6 hours a month for workflow improvements and small integrations</li><li>Accuracy check every month, against real examples</li><li>Monthly ROI report, quarterly roadmap review</li><li>Support: within 4 business hours</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card plan reveal">
            <h3>Partner</h3>
            <div class="plan__price">R35,000<small>/month</small></div>
            <p>For businesses running several systems: all of them looked after, with the fastest response.</p>
            <ul><li>All systems in the agreement</li><li>AI usage (what the AI provider charges) up to R10,000 a month</li><li>15 hours a month, unused hours roll over one month</li><li>Accuracy check every month, against real examples</li><li>Monthly ROI report and review call, monthly roadmap</li><li>Support: within 2 business hours; critical within 1</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="center small muted section__foot reveal">Model and API use above the allowance is billed at cost, and we warn you at 80%. Unused hours don&rsquo;t roll over, except on Partner (one month).</p>

        <div class="table-wrap reveal" id="sla" style="margin-top:2rem">
          <table class="spec spec--sla">
            <caption>Service levels</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Operate</th><th scope="col">Optimise</th><th scope="col">Partner</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Critical: down, or wrong outputs at scale</th><td>Next business day</td><td>4 business hours</td><td>1 business hour</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">High: a part failing, with a workaround</th><td>Next business day</td><td>4 business hours</td><td>2 business hours</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Normal: questions and requests</th><td>2 business days</td><td>Next business day</td><td>4 business hours</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Monitoring &amp; alerts</th><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Security updates &amp; maintenance</th><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Accuracy check</th><td>Quarterly</td><td>Monthly</td><td>Monthly</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted reveal" style="margin-top:0.8rem">Business hours are Monday to Friday, 08:00–17:00 SAST, excluding public holidays. Response time is a person acknowledging the issue with a first assessment, not a guaranteed fix time. We monitor the AI providers we use but can&rsquo;t guarantee their uptime; we guarantee how fast we respond and that your system falls back safely.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SEPARATE -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="separate" aria-labelledby="sepTitle">
      <div class="container split">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Priced separately</span>
          <h2 id="sepTitle">Outside the scope? It has a price before it starts.</h2>
          <p class="lead">This is what keeps implementation fixed and operations predictable. Small changes come out of your plan&rsquo;s hours first.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="price-list reveal">
          <li><span class="pl-name">Change requests<small>Beyond your plan&rsquo;s hours, quoted before work starts</small></span><span class="price">R1,250<span class="per">/hour</span></span></li>
          <li><span class="pl-name">New functionality<small>A new capability is its own project, with its own fixed quote</small></span><span class="price">Quoted</span></li>
          <li><span class="pl-name">Consulting &amp; workshops<small>Half-day workshop R7,500</small></span><span class="price">R1,850<span class="per">/hour</span></span></li>
          <li><span class="pl-name">Emergency support<small>Outside business hours, 1-hour minimum</small></span><span class="price">R2,450<span class="per">/hour</span></span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHAT AFFECTS COST / ONGOING -->
    <section class="section" id="cost" aria-labelledby="costTitle">
      <div class="container split">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">What affects the cost</span>
          <h2 id="costTitle">Scope, not surprises.</h2>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><b>Scope:</b> how many pages, screens, steps or users.</li>
            <li><b>Integrations:</b> how many systems it connects to, and whether they have a way in.</li>
            <li><b>Complexity:</b> the rules, exceptions and approvals it has to handle.</li>
            <li><b>Data:</b> whether your information is ready to use or needs cleaning first.</li>
            <li><b>Ongoing requirements:</b> how much support, monitoring and change you need afterwards.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal" id="ongoing">
          <span class="eyebrow">Ongoing costs</span>
          <h2>Listed in your proposal, never added later.</h2>
          <ul class="price-list price-list--compact">
            <li><span class="pl-name">Managed hosting<small>Secure, backed up and monitored · or R4,500 a year</small></span><span class="price">R450<span class="per">/month</span></span></li>
            <li><span class="pl-name">Care<small>Hosting plus an hour of changes, updates and a monthly report</small></span><span class="price">R1,450<span class="per">/month</span></span></li>
            <li><span class="pl-name">Third-party subscriptions<small>Software you choose to use, billed by the provider</small></span><span class="price">At cost</span></li>
            <li><span class="pl-name">AI usage<small>What the AI provider charges, passed through, never marked up</small></span><span class="price">At cost</span></li>
            <li><span class="pl-name">Support for larger AI systems<small>Monitoring, accuracy checks and improvements, with agreed response times</small></span><span class="price"><small>from</small>R7,500<span class="per">/month</span></span></li>
            <li><span class="pl-name">Future changes<small>Quoted before work starts</small></span><span class="price">R1,250<span class="per">/hour</span></span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PROCESS -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="process" aria-labelledby="procTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">How a project works</span>
          <h2 id="procTitle">You see the price before anything is built.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="steps steps--tight reveal">
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">1</span><h3>Tell us the problem</h3><p>In your own words. No technical terms needed.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">2</span><h3>We propose a solution</h3><p>We clarify the scope and suggest the simplest thing that works, which isn&rsquo;t always AI.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">3</span><h3>Fixed proposal &amp; deposit</h3><p>A fixed price before development. Approve it and pay a 40% deposit.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">4</span><h3>Build &amp; review</h3><p>You review it; agreed changes within the scope are included.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">5</span><h3>Pay the balance &amp; launch</h3><p>We launch or hand it over as agreed. You own it.</p></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="small muted section__foot reveal">Deposits, revisions, payment, ownership, handover and support are set out in the <a class="inline-link" href="terms">terms</a> before a project starts.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="pricingFaqTitle">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Pricing questions</span>
          <h2 id="pricingFaqTitle">Common questions about cost.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq reveal">
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What do I get at the starting price?</summary><p>A well-defined first project: a business website, a dashboard from your main systems, one automated workflow, one focused AI tool, or a focused custom tool. More pages, sources, integrations or users add to the price, and your proposal shows exactly what&rsquo;s included.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Why doesn&rsquo;t every project cost the starting price?</summary><p>Because a one-page site and a booking system with payments are both &ldquo;websites&rdquo;, but they&rsquo;re not the same work. Starting prices tell you where a project begins; the fixed proposal tells you what yours costs, before anything is built.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Why isn&rsquo;t discovery free?</summary><p>Because it&rsquo;s the most valuable part: a map of your processes, measured baselines and a scored list of opportunities. You keep it whether or not you build with us, and it&rsquo;s credited in full if you do within 60 days. The process review before it is free.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Can we stop after the proof of concept?</summary><p>Yes. That&rsquo;s what it&rsquo;s for. If the measured result doesn&rsquo;t justify production, we&rsquo;ll say so, and you&rsquo;ve only paid for the proof of concept.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Why is Operations a monthly fee?</summary><p>AI systems aren&rsquo;t finished at go-live. Models change, your processes change, and accuracy drifts if nobody checks it. Operations covers the model and API costs, monitoring, security, evaluation, support and improvements, and proves the value every month.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What if our AI usage goes above the allowance?</summary><p>We warn you at 80% of the allowance. Anything above it is billed at cost, never marked up. If it keeps happening, we&rsquo;ll suggest the plan or design change that brings it down.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Do you build websites?</summary><p>Yes, from R12,500 with a free design preview first, plus managed hosting and Care. They&rsquo;re priced and run separately from the AI work.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta" aria-labelledby="pricingCtaTitle">
      <div class="container cta__inner reveal">
        <h2 id="pricingCtaTitle">Have a question before committing?</h2>
        <p>Ask it. Tell us what you&rsquo;re trying to improve and we&rsquo;ll tell you honestly what it would cost, including the ongoing part.</p>
        <div class="btn-row btn-row--center">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--light btn--large" data-review-open data-track="cta-pricing-final">Tell us what&rsquo;s slowing you down</button>
          <a href="start" class="btn btn--ghost-light btn--large">Get an estimate</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
